      "problem_text": "Solve log_2 x + log_4 y = 3 and log_4 x + log_2 y = 5.",
      "answer": "x=16,y=128",
      "solution": "log_4 y = log_2 y / 2. So eq1: log_2 x + 0.5log_2 y = 3 => 2log_2 x + log_2 y = 6. Eq2: 0.5log_2 x + log_2 y = 5 => log_2 x + 2log_2 y = 10. Solve: let u=log_2 x, v=log_2 y. 2u+v=6, u+2v=10 => u=2/3, v=14/3... Let me redo: 2u+v=6, 0.5u+v=5... eq2: log_4 x + log_2 y = 5 => (1/2)u+v=5 => u+2v=10. Solve: 2u+v=6, u+2v=10 => from 1: v=6-2u. Sub: u+2(6-2u)=10 => u+12-4u=10 => -3u=-2 => u=2/3, v=6-4/3=14/3. x=2^{2/3}=cbrt(4), y=2^{14/3}",
      "marks": 4
    },
